{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #1103: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $A$ be an infinite sequence of integers such that every $n\\in A+A$ is squarefree. How fast must $A$ grow? Current best: In \\cite{Er81h} he asked whether there is an infinite sequence of integers $A$ such that, for every $a\\in A$ and prime $p$, if\\[a\\equiv t\\pmod{p^2}\\]then $1\\leq t<p^2/2$. A superior lower bound of $a_j \\gg j^{15/11-o(1)}$ had earlier been found by Konyagin \\cite{Ko04} when considering the finite case [1109]. Prize: no. OEIS: A392164. Tags: number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_06f972ff913a9caffbb6130ce4c3ab75dceee25341d0345260a4e06af9d5fd16","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1103","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_66a027900fa8c250","object_root":"sha256:68f90e352bdd812e3f4384268c214f2f5f147dc4933db0b54ed60bdaa93568ff","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1103"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema